  "title": "Perdikis2018: CNBI EPFL Cybathlon BCI-race motor-imagery dataset",
  "description": "EEG recordings from two tetraplegic pilots of team Brain Tweakers (CNBI, EPFL) during longitudinal motor-imagery BCI training for the Cybathlon 2016 BCI race. The dataset contains 16-channel EEG from cue-based offline calibration runs with three classes (both hands, both feet, rest), recorded at 512 Hz. It was re-released in BIDS format from the original Zenodo deposit via MOABB.",
  "methods_description": "16-channel EEG (Fz, FC3-FC4, C3-C4, CP3-CP4, etc.) was recorded with a g.USBamp amplifier (g.tec) using Ag/AgCl sensors at 512 Hz. Pilots performed cued kinesthetic motor imagery of both hands, both feet, or rest (4 s imagery after a 1 s cue) to control an avatar in the BrainRunners game. Runs were pooled across several recording days per pilot as a single session.",
